#
# Conformance case: foundation/free-role
# AC: foundation lowering — OntoUML FreeRole discipline (issue #503).
#
# Reproduces reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline: an anti-rigid sortal
# (logic:Role / logic:Phase) must specialize a rigid sortal so it has somewhere
# to inherit a principle of identity. ex:Wanderer is a logic:Role with NO rigid
# (Kind/SubKind) ancestor → logic:FreeRole. It is ALSO a non-Kind sortal tracing
# to ZERO Kind ancestors, so it additionally trips logic:MixIden — the FULL lint
# set, faithfully reproduced (identity_overlap fires independently of
# anti_rigidity_discipline). No instance is typed by ex:Wanderer, so the default
# witness-obligation policy emits no instance-level obligation.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the single
# stereotype pun is duplicated there in the named world ex:schema; this
# declaration is the program axiom the projections need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/free-role/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: a lone Role with no rigid parent (also asserted as a world fact in input.nq).
ex:Wanderer a logic:Role .
